  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bloomberg Data for Health Initiative Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bloomberg Philanthropies (BP) and the Australian Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) aim to build capacity to better utilise health data for policy development and application through the Data 4 Health (D4H) program. D4H aims to bring expert technical assistance from some of the world&#x2019;s leading public health organisations and academic institutions to support governments in 1) births and deaths: strengthening civil registration and vital statistics (CRVS) systems and improving information on cause of death; 2) data impact (DI): improving the capacity of country governments to use health data to inform policy development; and 3) selected other areas including a) noncommunicable diseases (NCDs) surveys, b) cancer registries and c) targeted subgrants for opportunistic support.</narrative>
  </description>
